The desk merged **412** unique reports into one ticket and marked it known: “parser reads month first.” The export’s own `causes.ts` splits those reports into **two** root causes. Intake tags and subject lines are guesses; the cause follows the **tenant locale** and the **booking form**.

This page replaces that single-cause claim. Counts are from `uniqueById` over `reports-4471.json` (427 raw rows → 412 unique ids; 15 overlapping export duplicates dropped). Sum: 379 + 33 = 412. Nothing left unplaced.

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 is not one bug. File and fix the two tickets below separately.
</Callout>

## Tickets

| cause | what breaks | Covers N reports | ticket |
| --- | --- | ---: | --- |
| `parser` | Shared parser reads every date month-first. Day-first tenants get month/day flipped. | 379 | [#1](https://github.com/arekczarny/what-it-shows/issues/1) |
| `hint` | booking-v3 prints an `MM/DD/YYYY` hint; the form reads day-first. People type the hint; the form flips it. | 33 | [#2](https://github.com/arekczarny/what-it-shows/issues/2) |

Report id lists: [`tickets/parser-report-ids.txt`](https://github.com/arekczarny/what-it-shows/blob/main/tickets/parser-report-ids.txt), [`tickets/hint-report-ids.txt`](https://github.com/arekczarny/what-it-shows/blob/main/tickets/hint-report-ids.txt).

## How to recognise each

**parser** — day-first tenant; channel `app`/`email`, or `form` on booking-v2 (or non-hint path on booking-v3). Symptom is a month/day swap, not only a one-day shift.

**hint** — day-first tenant; channel **`form`**; form **booking-v3**. Tenants: copper.studio, alder.physio, pale.harbour.

## What the desk got wrong

- The incident page said “one issue, one fix queued.” `CauseTable` against the same data shows two causes; `hint` had no ticket of its own.
- Triage still says merge on **subject** ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject), reviewed 2024-06-11). Same subject can be different causes (see `DedupeExplorer` / `sameCause`). That rule is stale relative to `causes.ts`.
- Five reports (`desk-notes.json` `oneDayMove`: R-41202, R-41209, R-41236, R-41344, R-41620) were read as one-day/timezone moves. By tenant they are still `parser`; they are footnoted under [#1](https://github.com/arekczarny/what-it-shows/issues/1), not a third ticket.
- The desk kept merging after the page was reviewed (2026-09-30): twelve more unique reports arrived through 2026-10-04 (export day). They are included in the 412 and fall under `parser`.

## Method

Classification matches `src/lib/kb/causes.ts` `causeOf` / `groupByCause` / `uniqueById`. Re-run from the working folder: `node classify-reports.mjs`.

